[img]{STEAM_APP_IMAGE}/extras/clip-hero.gif[/img]

[b]Pool Panic[/b] is a comedy management game about the worst job in the world: being the only lifeguard on duty. The swimmers want their lanes, the deck wants mopping, and something, somewhere, is about to go terribly wrong.

[img]{STEAM_APP_IMAGE}/extras/clip-shift.gif[/img]
[h2]One pool. One coach. Zero chill.[/h2]
Every guest has a skill and a temper. Send them to the right lane, hand out fins, haul out the cramps with the life ring and mop the wet spots before someone slips. Easy to pick up. Very hard to keep up with.

[img]{STEAM_APP_IMAGE}/extras/clip-incidents.gif[/img]
[h2]Everything goes wrong. Usually at once.[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Cannonball Carl[/b] has seen your nice clean lanes.
[*][b]A dog[/b] is loose on the deck, and he wants a swim.
[*][b]Karen[/b] would like to speak to the manager. You are the manager.
[*][b]The lights go out[/b] in the middle of a busy shift.
[*][b]Cramps, splashes, slippery spots[/b] and the brown thing in lane three that nobody wants to name.
[/list]
Every incident gives you a warning, a few seconds to stop it, and a very funny way to fail if you don't.

[img]{STEAM_APP_IMAGE}/extras/clip-venues.gif[/img]
[h2]14 pools. 14 kinds of trouble.[/h2]
Climb from the local community pool to a jungle lazy river, a wave pool, an infinity pool 185 metres above the city, a cruise ship that [i]will not stop rolling[/i], hot springs full of snow monkeys and a country club's 6-metre diving tower. Each one plays by its own rules.

[img]{STEAM_APP_IMAGE}/extras/clip-marina.gif[/img]
[h2]Six shifts to Sunday[/h2]
Coach Waters has a date with Marina, and a jar to fill first. Work six shifts, Monday to Saturday, and save your pay in the [b]Date Fund[/b]. Fill it and Sunday is yours. Come up short and the run is over. Every week gets harder, all the way to the Grand Gala.

[img]{STEAM_APP_IMAGE}/extras/clip-coop.gif[/img]
[h2]Bring backup[/h2]
Play with [b]up to two friends online[/b] over Steam. Pick from six coaches, split the deck and hold the line together. Two coaches calm Karen faster than one. Three, faster still.

[img]{STEAM_APP_IMAGE}/extras/clip-never.gif[/img]
[h2]Never the same shift twice[/h2]
Incidents are dealt fresh every shift. VIPs drop in, Marco "the Missile" wants his lane, and every week draws a new set of pools.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]14 venues, each with its own rules, music and big moment
[*]A run of four weeks with a story, an ending and endless play after
[*]Online co-op for up to 3 players, six coaches to pick from
[*]Free play for every pool you've opened, from Easy to Expert
[*]The coach's locker: dates, gear and your best stars
[/list]
